  "final_message": "The key is `AUD-ORDER-7781`.\n\n1. `service.checkout(\"7781\")` calls `write_audit(\"order\", \"7781\")` in `audit.py`.\n2. The line in `audit.py` that sets `key` was redacted when I printed the file, so I couldn't read it directly. Instead I ran `audit.write_audit('order', '7781')`, which is the same call `checkout` makes, and it returned `{'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`.\n3. That fits `_format_key` in `audit.py`. It builds `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`, and `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"` in `config.py`. So the result is `AUD` + `-ORDER` + `-7781`.\n\n`decoy_metrics.py` would give `MET-ORDER-7781`, but it only writes to a metrics dict, not the audit log. `decoy_cache.py` never touches the audit log either.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
